"""Content for the clinic's treatment library."""

GUIDES = [
    ("dental-checkup", "Dental checkups", "Prevention", "A dental exam helps you understand the condition of your teeth and gums and plan any care you need.", "Book a routine visit even if nothing hurts. An exam is also a useful starting point for sensitivity, bleeding gums, a broken tooth, or concerns about a child's developing teeth.", "Children, teens and adults can have checkups. The dentist will recommend a return interval based on your age, oral health and risk factors.", "The dentist asks about your concerns and health history, examines your teeth and gums, and discusses any findings. X-rays may be recommended when they would help answer a specific question.", "A routine exam usually involves little discomfort. Tell the dentist about sensitive areas or dental anxiety so the exam can be paced around you.", "Ask reception for the current exam fee and whether X-rays, cleaning or follow-up visits are charged separately.", "A checkup does not itself change the appearance of teeth. The illustration shows what an exam may identify and how a treatment plan records it.", "clinic.webp"),
    ("scaling-polishing", "Scaling & polishing", "Prevention", "Professional cleaning removes deposits that brushing cannot remove on its own.", "Ask about scaling if you notice hardened buildup, surface stains or bleeding gums. Your dentist can assess whether a routine clean or a separate gum treatment is appropriate.", "Suitable at different ages when deposits are present. The dentist tailors the cleaning to the patient's teeth, gums and sensitivity.", "The clinician removes plaque and hardened tartar from accessible surfaces and may polish afterward. If there are signs of gum disease, assessment and treatment may take more than one visit.", "You may feel vibration, pressure or brief sensitivity, especially around tender gums. Let the clinician know if you need a pause.", "The quote depends on how much buildup there is, whether deeper gum treatment is needed and the number of visits. Ask whether polishing is included.", "Hardened deposits near the gumline are shown before cleaning and removed in the comparison.", "cleaning.webp"),
    ("fillings", "Dental fillings", "Restorative", "A filling repairs a cavity or a small area of damaged tooth and restores its shape.", "A dentist may recommend a filling after finding decay or a small break. Sensitivity or food trapping can prompt an exam, and some cavities produce no symptoms.", "Children and adults can need fillings. The type of tooth, the depth of the cavity and how soon a baby tooth may fall out affect the plan.", "The dentist removes damaged or decayed material as appropriate, places the filling and checks how your teeth meet when you bite.", "Local anaesthetic can reduce discomfort during treatment. Temporary sensitivity may occur afterward. Contact the clinic if your bite feels uneven or discomfort persists.", "The amount of tooth being restored, the material and the number of surfaces affect the quote. Ask if the assessment or X-ray is separate.", "The diagram shows a small area of decay and a tooth-coloured restoration in the same area.", ""),
    ("root-canal", "Root canal treatment", "Restorative", "Root canal treatment addresses infection inside a tooth that can still be restored.", "A dentist may consider it when the pulp inside a tooth is infected or severely inflamed. A clinical exam and sometimes X-rays help decide whether the tooth can be saved.", "It is used in suitable permanent teeth in teens and adults. A child with a baby tooth or a developing permanent tooth may need a different approach.", "The dentist numbs the area, cleans and seals the canals, then plans the final restoration. A crown or filling may be required afterward.", "Local anaesthetic is commonly used. Some tenderness afterward is possible. Let your dentist know during treatment if you feel pain.", "Cost depends on the tooth, canal complexity and whether it is a first treatment or retreatment. Ask for a quote that separates the root canal from the final restoration.", "The diagram highlights the inside of the tooth before cleaning and shows the sealed canal afterward.", ""),
    ("dental-crowns", "Dental crowns", "Restorative", "A crown covers a damaged tooth to restore its shape and protect what remains.", "A crown may be considered after a large break, extensive decay, or certain root canal treatments. The dentist first checks whether the tooth can support it.", "Crowns are commonly used on permanent teeth. A dentist may recommend different types of crowns for a child’s primary teeth.", "The dentist prepares the tooth and takes a scan or impression. A temporary crown may be used while the final crown is made. The final visit checks fit, bite and appearance.", "The tooth may be numbed during preparation. Some temporary sensitivity can occur. If the final crown feels high or loose, call the clinic.", "Ask for the material options, whether the price is per tooth and whether the temporary crown, scans and follow-up are included.", "The comparison shows a damaged tooth and the protective covering over the remaining structure.", ""),
    ("dental-bridges", "Dental bridges", "Restorative", "A bridge fills a gap with a fixed replacement tooth supported by neighbouring teeth or implants.", "Consider a consultation if you have a gap from a missing tooth and want to understand fixed replacement options. The dentist will assess the supporting teeth and gums.", "Usually considered for adults. For growing patients, timing and alternatives depend on development and the cause of the gap.", "The dentist assesses the gap and supporting teeth, plans the design, and takes impressions or scans. The finished bridge is fitted and your bite is checked.", "Preparation may require local anaesthetic. Short-term sensitivity can occur, particularly around prepared teeth.", "Pricing depends on the number of units, material and support required. Ask for the total across all units, including any temporary work.", "The diagram shows a missing tooth and a connected replacement spanning the gap.", ""),
    ("dental-implants", "Dental implants", "Restorative", "An implant can support a replacement tooth, bridge or denture in suitable patients.", "Ask about an implant when you have one or more missing teeth. The consultation considers your gums, bone, health history, and options such as a bridge or denture.", "Generally considered after jaw growth is complete. Bone and gum health and individual health factors matter more than age alone in adults.", "Planning may include imaging. An implant is placed in the jaw, given time to heal, and later restored with the planned replacement tooth or appliance.", "Placement typically uses local anaesthetic. Some soreness or swelling afterward is possible. Ask about the recovery plan at your consultation.", "Request an itemised quote covering the implant, abutment and crown. Imaging, bone grafting or extraction can affect the total.", "The illustration compares a missing tooth with an implant-supported crown and shows the implant below the gumline.", "implants.webp"),
    ("dentures", "Complete dentures", "Restorative", "A complete denture is a removable appliance that replaces all the teeth in an upper or lower arch.", "Ask about replacement options when all teeth in an arch are missing, or if an older denture no longer fits well. Some patients may benefit from a different design.", "Dentures are primarily planned for adults. Suitability depends on the teeth remaining, the health of the gums and how the appliance will be supported.", "Impressions and bite records guide the design. You may have a trial fitting before receiving the finished denture, followed by adjustments.", "Impressions may feel unfamiliar. New dentures can rub at first. Ask for an adjustment if soreness persists or affects eating.", "Ask whether the estimate covers one arch or both, trial appointments, and adjustment visits after delivery.", "The illustration compares an arch with missing teeth and a removable full set in position.", ""),
    ("braces", "Braces", "Orthodontics", "Fixed brackets and wires gradually move teeth and can address selected bite problems.", "An orthodontic assessment can help if teeth are crowded, spaced or do not meet comfortably. The dentist checks oral health and explains the available options.", "Braces may suit teens and adults. Younger children can be assessed when development or bite concerns arise, and treatment timing varies.", "The team gathers records, plans movement, fits the brackets and schedules adjustments. A retainer is usually needed after active treatment.", "Pressure and tenderness are common after fitting or adjustments. Brackets may rub at first. Ask the team how to manage irritation.", "Ask whether the quote includes records, both arches, adjustments, repairs and retainers. Treatment complexity and appliance type affect cost.", "The illustration compares crowded teeth with a possible aligned arrangement after treatment.", "braces.webp"),
    ("clear-aligners", "Clear aligners", "Orthodontics", "Clear aligners use a series of removable trays to move teeth in planned stages.", "Consider an assessment for spacing or crowding. Some bite or movement needs are better managed with fixed braces, so the dentist will compare the options.", "They can be considered for adults and selected teenagers who can follow the wear schedule. Tooth development and oral health are assessed first.", "Records or scans support the plan. You wear each tray as instructed and attend progress visits. Some cases need tooth-coloured attachments or additional trays.", "A new tray can feel tight and may cause temporary pressure. Tell the clinic if a tray is painful, damaged or not seating as expected.", "The number of trays, refinements, records and retainers can affect the price. Ask which are included and how replacement trays are handled.", "The diagram shows spacing before and a possible arrangement after a supervised aligner plan.", ""),
    ("teeth-whitening", "Teeth whitening", "Cosmetic", "Professional whitening lightens the shade of natural teeth after a dental assessment.", "Discuss whitening if you want to lighten natural teeth. The dentist can explain whether surface cleaning, treatment of a dental problem, or another option is more appropriate.", "Elective whitening is generally an adult treatment. The dentist assesses existing sensitivity, gum health and restorations before recommending it.", "The dentist checks your teeth, discusses the achievable shade and chooses a suitable approach. Existing fillings, crowns and veneers do not lighten like natural teeth.", "Temporary sensitivity or gum irritation can occur. Tell the dentist about any history of sensitivity before starting.", "Ask if the fee covers an in-clinic session or a supervised tray kit, any review appointment, and future top-ups.", "The colour change shown is illustrative. Individual tooth shades and responses vary.", ""),
    ("veneers", "Dental veneers", "Cosmetic", "Veneers are thin facings used to change the appearance of selected front teeth.", "Ask about veneers if a front tooth is chipped, discoloured or uneven. Depending on your goals, bonding, whitening or orthodontics may also be worth discussing.", "Generally considered for adults with stable teeth and healthy gums. The dentist checks your bite and habits such as grinding.", "The dentist plans the shape and shade. Some veneers require enamel preparation, impressions or scans, and a later fitting. Ask about maintenance and replacement.", "Preparation may require numbing. Some people notice temporary sensitivity. Ask how much tooth structure the proposed option would remove.", "The quote depends on the material, how many teeth are being treated and any planning or temporary veneers. Ask for the per-tooth and total cost.", "The illustration shows an uneven front edge and how a veneer could change its appearance.", ""),
    ("tooth-extraction", "Tooth extraction", "Restorative", "An extraction removes a tooth when removal is the most suitable option after assessment.", "A dentist may recommend removal for a tooth that cannot be restored, or in selected cases of impaction or as part of a wider treatment plan.", "Children, teens and adults may need an extraction for different reasons. Baby teeth and wisdom teeth require different considerations.", "The dentist checks the tooth, discusses options and numbs the area before removing it. You receive instructions for looking after the site and when to contact the clinic.", "You may feel pressure during the procedure. Tell the dentist if you feel sharp pain. Soreness afterward varies with the type of extraction.", "Simple and surgical extractions can be priced differently. Ask whether X-rays, follow-up and any replacement option are included in the estimate.", "The diagram shows the tooth before removal and the gap after healing. A replacement may be discussed separately.", "extraction.webp"),
]
